      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues: unused imports, vague field names, and trailing-space assertion messages. I'll write an improved version.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused imports, renamed the vague `TEST_BOM_1/2/3` fields to descriptive `SINGLE_BYTE_BOM`, `TWO_BYTE_BOM`, and `THREE_BYTE_BOM`, added brief field-level Javadoc, and replaced the trailing-space assertion messages with clear, sentence-form descriptions — all without changing the tested methods, arguments, or expected values."
    }
